    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nRunning this script \n```lua\n_G.debug = nil\nvim.schedule(function() end)\nvim.wait(100)\n```\ncauses unexpected failure \n```bash\nE5113: Lua chunk: attempt to index a nil value\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'loop_poll'\n        [string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:176: in function 'wait'\n        crash.lua:3: in main chunk\nPANIC: unprotected error in call to Lua API (attempt to index a nil value)\n```\nreproduced in nightly\n```\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1418+gf97bcbdf77\nBuild type: RelWithDebInfo\nLuaJIT 2.1.1787165859\n```\n\nthe issue might be in src/nvim/lua/executor.c:322\nint nlua_pcall(lua_State *lstate, int nargs, int nresults)\n{\n  lua_getglobal(lstate, \"debug\");\n  lua_getfield(lstate, -1, \"traceback\"); <-- fails if debug is nil \n\nnlua_pcall wraps lots of callbacks e.g., vim.schedule, so scripts manipulating `debug` can degrade functionality.\n\nLet me know if you would like a pull request (was thinking to cache debug.traceback in LUA_REGISTRYINDEX before any usercode runs but not sure if that breaks any existing contracts e.g., is usercode allowed to enhance traceback?)  \n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nsee above\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nno error\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1418+gf97bcbdf77\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot tested\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.6.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nNA\n\n### Installation\n\ndownloaded from GitHub release",
