            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> that was an extreme example; a more likely risk (as was in my case) is an imported module that replaces debug with its own implementation. \n\nThat causes an error in a different location though. nlua is **never** going to be a perfect sandbox (only vimscript has such delusions), you can always get it to crash nvim in some way. therefore it is much more useful to report the _original_ error with some of the original context (overriding some parts of `debug` is expected to be fine, straight up **deleting the stdlib** is not), not \"reducing\" it to another case of \"ZOMG I got nvim to crash\" without the useful information.",
